File: vUX-formComponents.js

=======================================================================
Section 1 — module imports
OLD_SECTION
import { validateArray, validateObjectLiteral, validateString } from "./src/helpers.js";
import "./src/vUX-core-4.0.0-beta.js";

NEW_SECTION
import { validateArray, validateObjectLiteral, validateString } from "./src/helpers.js";
import "./src/vUX-core-4.0.0-beta.js";
import { FormValidator } from "./vUX-formValidator.js";
import { ListScroller } from "./vUX-listScroller.js";

REASON
datePicker calls FormValidator.format.integerField() (datetime-local hour/minute
formatting) and new ListScroller() (decade-series scroller), but neither constructor was
imported and neither module attaches itself to window, so both calls threw
ReferenceError — opening any default-range (1900–2050) date picker crashed, as did
building any datetime-local picker. Both modules were verified to have no import-time
side effects (their CSS is linked inside initialize()) and no circular imports.

=======================================================================
Section 2 — select: builder state
OLD_SECTION
var selectDim = [], selectIcon = "",labelAttribute="", wrapperStyle = "",toolTipHandler = null,enableToolTip = false,selectFieldStyle = "", optionStyle = "", selectClassName = "", ...

NEW_SECTION
var selectDim = [], selectIcon = "",labelAttribute="", wrapperStyle = "",toolTipHandler = null,enableToolTip = false,selectFieldStyle = "", optionStyle = "", optionGroupStyle = "", selectClassName = "", ...

REASON
The config.optionGroupStyle setter assigned to optionGroupStyle, which was never
declared in the select closure; in strict module scope the assignment threw a
ReferenceError. Declared it alongside the other style strings.

=======================================================================
Section 3 — select: autoPlace()
OLD_SECTION
(three placement lines using) (parseInt(selectDim[1]) + 1) + "px"

NEW_SECTION
var wrapperHeight = optionsCon.parentNode.offsetHeight; //this widget's own rendered height, not the last-built widget's config
(three placement lines using) (wrapperHeight + 1) + "px"

REASON
selectDim is builder-level state overwritten on every build, so the dropdown of every
select was offset by the height of the LAST-built select. Placement now measures the
widget's own rendered wrapper height.

=======================================================================
Section 4 — select: getOptionsConHeight()
OLD_SECTION
return height = includeSearchField ? height + (parseInt(selectDim[0]) + 5) : height + 5;

NEW_SECTION
return height = includeSearchField ? height + (optionsCon.parentNode.offsetHeight + 5) : height + 5; //search box is one field-height tall

REASON
Same shared-state problem as Section 3, compounded by a width/height mixup:
selectDim[0] is the widget WIDTH, while the search box's height is the field height
(the generated CSS sets .sSearchBox::before height to selectDim[1]). The estimate that
decides whether the list opens upward or downward was inflated by the widget's width.

=======================================================================
Section 5 — select: selectStyleSheet()
OLD_SECTION
if (optionStyle != "") css += ".v" + selectClassName + " .sOptionCon .sOption{" + optionStyle + "}";

NEW_SECTION
if (optionStyle != "") css += ".v" + selectClassName + " .sOptionCon .sOption{" + optionStyle + "}";
if (optionGroupStyle != "") css += ".v" + selectClassName + " .sOptionCon .sOptionGroup{" + optionGroupStyle + "}"; //optgroup label rows

REASON
config.optionGroupStyle was accepted (see Section 2) but its value was never emitted
into the generated stylesheet; it now styles the .sOptionGroup rows.

