=======================================================================
Section 9 — datePicker: builder state
OLD_SECTION
var tooTipHandler = null,dateInputIconStyle = [],daysToolTip = false, ...

NEW_SECTION
var toolTipHandler = null,dateInputIconStyle = [],daysToolTip = false, ...

REASON
The variable was declared with a typo (tooTipHandler) while autoBuild assigned
toolTipHandler — an undeclared identifier, which throws in strict module scope, so the
daysToolTip feature never initialized. Normalized to toolTipHandler everywhere
(see Sections 11 and 12).

=======================================================================
Section 10 — datePicker: autoPlace()
OLD_SECTION
(three placement lines using) (parseInt(datePickerDim[1]) + 1) + "px"

NEW_SECTION
var wrapperHeight = wrapper.offsetHeight; //this widget's own rendered height, not the last-built widget's config
(three placement lines using) (wrapperHeight + 1) + "px"

REASON
Same shared-dimension bug as the select (Section 3): with mixed-size pickers the panel
was offset by the last-built picker's height. datePicker sets per-widget inline sizes,
so measuring the wrapper is exact.

