Section 11 — datePicker: month click handler, February day count
OLD_SECTION
} else if (month == "2") {
    var leapYear = parseInt(dateComponents[0]) % 4;
    if (leapYear == 0) {
        stopDay = 28;
    } else {
        stopDay = 27;
    }
}

NEW_SECTION
} else if (month == "2") {
    var year = parseInt(dateComponents["dateParts"][0]);
    var leapYear = (year % 4 == 0 && year % 100 != 0) || year % 400 == 0;
    if (leapYear) {
        stopDay = 28;
    } else {
        stopDay = 27;
    }
}

REASON
dateComponents[0] is undefined (the year lives at dateComponents["dateParts"][0]), so
the modulo was NaN and February always rendered 28 days, never 29, in every year. Also
upgraded the %4-only rule to the full Gregorian leap-year rule (century years).

